 13.2 Confidentiality.  A Party may not disclose the terms of any OPA to a third party (other than the Party’s and its affiliates’ lenders, counsel, accountants, or  prospective assignee (but only as to OPAs to be assigned), in each case that have agreed to keep the terms confidential) except to comply with any applicable law, order, regulation, or exchange rule; provided, however, each Party shall notify the other Party of any proceeding of which it is aware that may result in disclosure and use reasonable efforts to prevent or limit the disclosure.  The provisions of this Agreement (other than the terms of any OPA) are not subject to this confidentiality obligation.  The Parties shall be entitled to all remedies available at law or in equity to enforce, or seek relief in connection with, this confidentiality obligation; provided, however, that all monetary damages shall be limited to actual direct damages.


